branch('WB19',[(194,1,16),(194,47,56)],'Draft identity, repeated first-line exercise and owner preservation','REPORT.WKB is supplied first draft, separate from earlier learner OUTLINE. Step3 covers every remaining paragraph first line but excludes titles and the existing table. Source does not enumerate paragraph count, so no finite per-paragraph case count is invented. Optional Reveal Codes must preserve beginning-of-line owners; vertical moves try to preserve horizontal cursor position.','L3 I4 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB19',[(195,4,22),(195,53,55),(196,1,17),(196,48,53),(197,1,2)],'Temporary paragraph margins versus literal tabs','A leading Tab affects only first line; F4 left Indent moves all wrapped paragraph lines to next stop. Backspace removes that owner before Shift+F4 bilateral Indent; two quotation paragraphs each receive another bilateral indent, adding half inch at each side. Enter ends temporary paragraph margin; no equivalent chain of literal tabs or permanent margin edits is inferred.','L3 E1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB19',[(195,18,21),(196,1,5),(196,15,17)],'WB19 later indent notice','WBC51 notice3 records12/90 corrections to steps4,6,10: F4 for left indent and Shift+F4 for both margins. Original arrow-decorated labels are visually read as native indent icons and kept separate from later wording. No executable observation.','L3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB19',[(197,4,34)],'Persistent spacing and three repeated exceptions','Set1.5 at report beginning; for two quotation paragraphs and Operating Expenses table set1 at beginning and1.5 after last line. These are three distinct target regions within numbered step8, each needing both boundary owners. Table begins at its title; preserving paragraph indent and surrounding spacing is part of the branch.','L3 P3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB19',[(198,1,10),(198,42,54),(199,34,38)],'Underline state, selected tabs and local reset alternative','Underline selected column-title line initially affects words/spaces but not tabs. Set Underline Spaces/Tabs at document beginning, retaining spaces Yes and choosing tabs Yes. Document-wide owner then affects all later underlined tabs. Optional table-only setup would add before/after owners; no exact reset keystrokes are supplied. Left-drag selection and Font/Appearance/Underline are separate routes.','L1 L3 I3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB19',[(199,40,54)],'Preview, first learner save and persistent versus paragraph formats','Page through View Document, exit preview, save learner REPORT and stay in application with cleared screen. Original REPORT.WKB stays distinct. Prose contrasts paragraph-ending Indent with persistent Line Spacing; exact output pagination depends on draft, resource metrics and all prior edits.','P3 L1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB20',[(200,7,36),(201,1,10),(201,12,30),(205,1,27)],'Contradictory introductory illustration order','Initial examples printed191/192/196 show Mail Order then Retail, while numbered input printed192–194 creates Retail then Mail Order; column-swap exercise later intentionally changes order. WBC51 notices1683/2079 reverse early screenshots/title, but1683 declares pages186–187 and2079page191. Keep notice page claims and actual1989 locators separate; do not globally reverse all illustrations or future inputs.','L3 L1 P3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB20',[(201,31,36),(202,1,43)],'Tab ruler formats, decimal input and dot leader','Clear existing stops, add relative3/5in and change both L to D; period marks first D as leader. Left/Center/Right/Decimal are visible options; Center and Flush Right/Tab Align command analogy does not execute every format. During typing digits move left until decimal point; leader is generated from tab definition rather than typed periods.','L3 L1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB20',[(202,45,52),(203,1,9)],'Complete guided quarter-row exercise','Step3 repeats table entry for Q2/Q3/Q4; structured exercise rows separately retain all retail/mail amounts. First row belongs to steps1/2. Source step3 says use steps2 and3 as guide, a self-reference retained as ambiguity rather than silently changing to1/2.','L3 L1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB20',[(203,38,43),(204,1,1),(204,31,49)],'Definition scope and restoring normal tabs','Decimal definition persists beyond table and changes following paragraph-leading tab presentation. Insert new definition after final data line; clear ruler;0,.5 restores half-inch interval from margin; later paragraph becomes normal Tab again. Prose Align conflicts with illustrated Dec Tab and later notice1850; preserve documentary labels without asserting native bytes.','L3 E1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB20',[(205,18,36),(206,1,17),(206,43,52),(207,1,5)],'Absolute measurement, resource-dependent coordinates and relative definition','Positions4.3/6.3in measured after first-row figures are from page edge; initial left margin1in yields relative3.3/5.3in. Absolute ruler removes signs and starts at page0; absolute title stops remain fixed when left margin changes, relative data stops move. Numeric examples require font/printer metrics and exact table input.','L3 L1 I4 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB20',[(207,7,18)],'Title attributes and native tab-code editions','Bold+Underline title text uses Right tabs.1989 prose calls generic Align/Center, while illustrated native labels include Rt Tab/Dec Tab. WBC51notice36412/90 uses Rgt Tab/Cntr Tab, including its assertion about figure columns. Do not force these prose variants into one native encoding or infer every format has same owner.','L1 L3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB20',[(207,20,36),(208,1,5)],'Preview alternatives and table-local spacing','Inspect Full Page and100%; set spacing1 at heading and reset1.5 after table. Three numbered spacing steps preserve source granularity despite broader prose calling them next two steps. No preview or print execution is claimed.','P3 L3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB20',[(208,7,24),(209,1,25),(210,32,38)],'Optional failed centering attempts and margin-owner order','Source invites trying Center on each table line or Tab; expected last tab/text spills next line. Guided route sets table left1.5in, keeps right1in; replaces absolute title definition with relative3.3/5.3 then deletes obsolete owner; below table resets left1in. Figures shift before title fix; initial4.3/6.3 absolute values are not converted using new1.5 margin because desired title positions shift too.','L3 E1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB20',[(210,40,53),(211,1,8),(211,38,45)],'Tabular-column selection and menu bypass','Initial linear Block may highlight unwanted text; Move/Tabular Column resolves entire Retail column by selection endpoints. Menu alternative Edit/Select/Tabular Column skips keyboard steps2/3 and resumes step4. Move carries tabs/attributes and definition owner; insertion after Mail Order switches actual column data and generated leader assignment. Cancel/refusal and payload outside chosen column remain unobserved.','L3 E1 I3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB20',[(212,31,46)],'Displaced tab definition and bounded Undelete','Delete displaced relative title-definition owner, triple Home/Left to first code gap, Cancel/Restore restores it. Cancel here opens Undelete; it is not evidence of cancelling an active move. Source says history holds last three deletions; fourth-oldest loss and failure/cancel paths need independent original evidence. Prose advises Move for relocation to avoid history eviction.','L3 E1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB20',[(213,28,39),(214,1,3),(214,33,36),(214,64,69)],'Paired-attribute cleanup and retained text range','Column move preserves Bold and Underline using separate pairs; block whole title line then Bold consolidates Bold, Block/Go To twice reselects line then Underline consolidates Underline. Replacing table heading occurs inside Bold pair; native owners and unselected data must survive, not merely matching screen typography.','L1 E1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB20',[(215,30,47)],'Page navigation, delayed menu icon and overwrite','Try cursor keys/Go To Up or Down in preview; menu Print icon appears after navigation step2 but routes Print opening step1. Save existing REPORT with replacement Yes, then clear screen; overwrite refusal/cancel/failed writes remain pending, not numbered source steps.','P3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB21',[(216,7,27),(217,1,9),(217,40,45)],'Footer page marker, preview navigation typo and display branch','Footer A Every Page contains report label, Flush Right, Page prefix and inserted special page-number marker.1989 printed207 step2 visually reverses PgUp/PgDn abbreviations beside Page Down/Page Up. Go To number1 and100%/200% display branches remain distinct;200% may be needed on CGA. Numbered footnote is placed above footer.','P3 L8 L1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB21',[(217,45,55),(218,1,15),(218,47,50)],'Footer-hosted graphic line, fractional input and margin precedence','Edit Footer A, create horizontal line with width1/18in and50% gray, Enter twice before footer text. Later recreated footer uses.056in, an explicit rounded numeric input retained separately. Width responds to report margins only if margin owner precedes Footer owner. Footer line is native graphic entity in nested context; font/printer/preview support still required.','G3 P3 L1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB21',[(218,52,56),(219,1,37),(220,1,32)],'Odd/even footer repeat and wrong-footer recovery','Delete old Every Page Footer A, recreate A/Odd with right number; repeat steps3–11 as B/Even with number at left. Facing Pages shows even on left and odd on right; report page2 has no footer until B exists. If no page2 footer, source suggests wrong A or Odd selection; delete that Footer owner and retry. No finite full left-footer typing sequence is supplied, so retain required arrangement and repeat-template substitutions without inventing steps.','G3 P3 E1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB21',[(221,1,20),(221,51,53),(222,1,3)],'Footnote nested editing and owner expansion','Create note after comma near defeat; separate editor provides note number; enter citation with newsletter title underlined. Body shows marker2 and Reveal Codes exposes note text prefix. Marker/native owner, text and emphasis remain bound; source says most footer editing features available but does not execute all commands inside note.','L8 L10 L1 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB21',[(222,44,62),(223,1,1),(223,31,34)],'Earlier insertion renumbers existing notes and reflows body','Add page5 Ibid reference after first sentence, before just-created citation. Both temporarily display2; Down twice reformat changes later note to3. Preview displays notes1,2,3 and moves displaced body to page2. Note anchor ordering, transient display, note numbering and page-layout reflow are separate observations pending native/resource-qualified replay.','L8 L10 P3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB21',[(223,36,47)],'Edit-by-number and body-caret return','Footnote Edit1 can be invoked anywhere in document; replacing citation page39 with40 then Exit returns immediately right of note1 anchor, not caller location. Missing number/edit refusal/cancel are not specified.','L8 L10 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB21',[(223,49,53),(224,1,11),(224,40,54),(225,1,6)],'Searching Endnote owners and independent numbering methods','Search constructs Endnote/Note token through Footnote key, moves to note1 then next2; Reveal Codes differentiates nearby footnote4. Endnote Options contains spacing/keep-together/numbering leads, but guided route selects Letters only. Search twice after reset finds lettered first/second endnotes. No endnote creation or generation command is executed by these steps; notes were already in supplied draft.','L9 L10 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB21',[(225,30,36),(226,1,4),(226,36,52),(227,1,2)],'Endnote final-page placement and independent initial formats','Endnotes appear at document end only in preview/print, not at body anchors. Add Hard Page and centered Bold Endnotes title at report end to separate notes; do not invent generation step. Separate header/footer/note editors start with initial formats, so notes remain single spaced while body is1.5 until locally changed. Exact initial settings/resource context remain prerequisite.','L9 L10 L1 P3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
branch('WB21',[(227,4,12),(227,26,36),(228,1,19),(228,51,53)],'Whole-table protection, soft boundaries and mouse routes','Add spacing around expense table; comparison table straddles soft page break. Select from before all table heading owners to line below table and Format/Yes creates paired Block Protect owners. Source expects soft break moved above whole table; text subsequently inserted inside owners is also protected. Mouse positioning and left-drag selection are separately documented. A Hard Page would relocate once without guaranteeing all later soft-break protection.','L3 I3 E1 P3 Q1 Q2 Q3')
